donald trump has been the central figure  in a culture war in america  over whether or not to wear a face mask  in the pandemic  for that reason this was a significant  moment  for the first time ever the president  seen wearing a face mask  in public in accordance with his own  government's guidance  on a visit to a military hospital in  washington  on closer inspection his mask came  complete with a presidential seal  on his way he'd explained why the change  of approach  i think when you're in a hospital  especially in that particular setting  where you're talking to a lot of  soldiers and people that in some cases  just got off the operating tables  i think it's a great thing to wear a  mask i've never been against masks  but i do believe they have a time and a  place  it was only three months ago he  announced that government guidance  and then said he'd ignore it it's  voluntary you don't have to do it  they suggest it for a period of time  but uh this is voluntary  i don't think i'm going to be doing it  the man who wants to take his job has  been conspicuous in his adherence to the  guidance  and joe biden's campaign again  criticized the president  in a statement they said rather than  taking responsibility and leading  he wasted four months that americans  have been making sacrifices  by stoking divisions and actively  discouraging people from taking a very  basic step  to protect each other all the while the  number of new cases in the us continues  to break records  as states like florida are pushing ahead  with their reopening  disney world in orlando the most popular  theme park in the world  has started accepting visitors again  florida has recorded 500 deaths  in the last week alone hospitals are  approaching capacity  in a number of states and experts warn  the numbers will only rise  it's an uncomfortable position for a  president accused of mismanaging the  crisis  and keen to declare america on the road  to recovery  and whose chances of a second term  probably depend on it  greg milam sky news los angeles
 

